{#
Template: Unbordered List Group

Description:
This template renders an unbordered Bootstrap list group (`ul.list-group`).
Each list item contains an icon, a label, an optional value, and an optional content section.

Available Variables:
- list (array, required): An array of items, each containing:
    - icon (string, required): The CSS class for the icon (e.g., FontAwesome or Bootstrap icons).
    - label (string, required): The main label text for the list item.
    - value (string, optional): A value displayed on the right side.
    - content (string, optional): Additional content displayed below the label.
    - contentClass (string, optional): Additional CSS classes for the `content` paragraph.

Example Usage:

```twig
{% set items = [
    { icon: 'fas fa-user', label: 'Username', value: 'JohnDoe' },
    { icon: 'fas fa-envelope', label: 'Email', value: 'john@example.com' },
    { icon: 'fas fa-info-circle', label: 'Notes', content: 'This user is an admin.', contentClass: 'text-muted' }
] %}
{% include '@EMSAdminUI/bootstrap5/components/bootstrap/list-group.html.twig' with { list: items } %}
```
#}
<ul class="list-group list-group-unbordered">
{% for item in list %}
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <div class="d-flex w-100 justify-content-between">
            <b><i class="{{ item.icon }}"></i> {{ item.label }}</b>
            {% if item.value is defined %}<span>{{ item.value }}</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        {% if item.content is defined %}
            <p class="mt-1 mb-0 {{ item.contentClass|default('') }}">
                {{ item.content }}
            </p>
        {% endif %}
    </li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>